            "body": "**Codex bot review · model: `gpt-6-astra`**\n\nReviewed `6ddc88558978` against base `97b7bc3128d6`.\n\nThank you for your contribution! The runtime guards prevent both missing-symbol lookups on older backends. I found no defect in this change. Approval is deferred while workflow approval and applicable CI remain pending.\n\nValidation: Compiled the exact head and baseline shim headers in C++17. Dynamic test libraries advertising versions below 9.22 and omitting both convolution symbols give NOT_SUPPORTED on the head; the baseline throws missing-symbol errors. Three old-version values were checked for both wrappers. At the 9.22 boundary and a later version, both revisions preserve all pointer, dimension, dtype and activation arguments and return the stub backend status unchanged. Direct-link controls below and at the boundary also pass: 12 process configurations and 24 wrapper assertions total. Checked the declaration/definition match, lookup ordering, Python status mapping and later causal-convolution wrappers. Precheck found no candidates. Strict pedantic compilation reports the same two unrelated variadic-macro diagnostics on head and baseline.\n\nLimitations: These are host shim tests with controlled libraries, not native convolution tests or a real old-backend qualification. No full Python extension rebuild or performance result is claimed. Style and Security require maintainer approval. The applicable python/misc CI route remains held after its known pre-test authentication failure; no retry or alternate route was used.\n\nReview incomplete; approval is deferred.\n\n<!-- codex-fe-review:v2:2214:6ddc8855897883cedd3f2419ceb629b30a1252d4:deferred:no-blocker -->",
